The `s.readRawData(pixel, pixel_size)` return value is not checked. If the stream is at end or has insufficient data, `pixel` may contain uninitialized data, which then gets copied into the image buffer. This uninitialized data is later used when converting to the internal format, causing the MSAN "Use-of-uninitialized-value" crash.

Let me create a TGA file that triggers this. I need:
- A valid TGA header (18 bytes)
- Image type 10 (RLE RGB) or 9 (RLE indexed) or 11 (RLE grey)
- A packet header with the RLE bit set (0x80)
- But insufficient data for the pixel bytes

